The Linux repair workflow builds pplpy against Sage's shared PPL and GMP
prefix.  Give that binary-compatible but materially different wheel a local
version so dependency resolution cannot silently replace it with upstream's
statically linked Linux wheel.  That wheel exports its private GMP symbols
globally and can interpose on FLINT's lazy GMP bindings in Sagelite.

diff --git a/meson.build b/meson.build
--- a/meson.build
+++ b/meson.build
@@ -5 +5 @@
-    version: '0.9.0',
+    version: '0.9.0.post1',
